This program will log the illuminance every 5 seconds to the file "light_log.txt". It will continue to do so until it receives a SIGINT signal (like pressing Ctrl+C). If any I2C write or read errors occur, or if the sensor is not present, the program will print an error message and exit. The program ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path.
Please note that you need to have the I2C interface enabled on your Raspberry Pi and the BH1750FVI sensor connected to the correct pins (GPIO2/GPIO3 with ADDR tied to GND).
Also, you need to have the necessary permissions to access the I2C bus and the file system. You can add your user to the i2c group to get the necessary permissions.
```
sudo usermod -a -G i2c $USER
```
Then, log out and log back in for the changes to take effect.
```
sudo reboot
```
