This program can be compiled with `gcc -o sunset_simulator sunset_simulator.c -lpigpio -lpthread -lrt -lm`. It can be run with `./sunset_simulator <duration>`, replacing `<duration>` with the desired duration in seconds. The program will print status messages to the console and handle SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to gracefully terminate the program.
Please note that you need to have the pigpio library installed on your Raspberry Pi Zero W to compile and run this program. You can install it with `sudo apt-get install pigpio`.
